You are in the equipment storage bay, sitting on an upturned crate with a manifest you have decided not to read. A strategy you once built, step by careful step, has been sitting in your head all week, and you are pressing it down the way you press down a lid that keeps lifting. On the shelf above you, a small many-legged creature, grey, striped, and of no species you can name, has made a nest in a coil of spare cabling. It regards you with what you can only call professional interest. You tell it the plan is not up for discussion. It rearranges two of its legs, which is more than the plan has managed lately.

