"The courier left on the second watch, and she wasn't alone," Vance Oduya says, tapping a line in his berth log. He turns the screen toward you. A tug pilot logged her departure, a fuel receipt places her at the outer dock, and a second hull lifted out a half hour behind. You copy the transponder tag onto the back of the manifest. On the shelf above, the creature leans over the edge of its cabling nest. Vance squints at the shelf. "Is that thing on the books?"

