Vance's finger stops on the screen. "Buying berths," he says, flat as the log. "Nobody's offered me a credit, and I'd remember the insult." He scrolls back one entry, then another, and his jaw works. "Second hull's tag matches a berth lease filed under a holding company. I don't know the name." Above you, the creature drops a length of cable onto the manifest. Vance asks, "Where did you hear this?"

