Bleakhold Station's observation lounge is mostly empty at this hour, the long window showing nothing worth the trouble of looking at. A hauler sits alone at one of the tables, turning a heavy bracelet over in the light, tilting it to check the weight against what he was told it was worth. Behind him, a scorched cutting torch lies abandoned on a service cart, its nozzle still faintly orange, the cart parked where someone meant to come back for it. The hauler weighs the bracelet once more and holds it up to the glass, as if the stars might give him a second opinion.

