Vance Oduya sits alone at the berth console on the dock at Bleakhold Station, the one log screen turned to the wall, and reads the lease filing again. It is the same holding company he did not recognise, and the same signature at the bottom. A notice from the Ascendancy has arrived overnight, polite and brief, naming his berths and a date. The courier's trail was only ever a small thing next to this, and the date makes it urgent. He does not delete the notice; he does not answer it either.

